WEBVTT

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.860
I'm sorry, Yusei.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.480
I couldn't do anything.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.350
That's not true!

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.480
Lua is right.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.870
I understand your passion.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.990
Leave the rest to me.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.010
But what a situation!

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.440
Who could've expected this?

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:27.070
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:32.570
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:37.040
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.880
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:47.850
There's no need to fear

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:55.530
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.530
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:07.270
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:12.680
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:20.790
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:52.620
Cornered  Last Wheeler Yusei

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.810
In a big surprise, tournament favorite Team 
5D's has started with consecutive losses!

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:02.490
The WRGP preliminaries are in chaos!

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.880
According to the rules, Speed Counters and

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.840
the cards on the field pass 
on to the next player!

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.430
Aki Izayoi used her remaining 
strength to protect

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.560
Stardust Dragon, so it passes 
on to the last wheeler Yusei!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:27.480
Aki, I won't let Stardust 
or your hopes go to waste!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.780
Well done.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.610
I couldn't do anything.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:51.270
Andore's strategy overwhelmed me, and it took 
everything I had to keep Stardust Dragon on the field.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:04:00.590
I talked a big game to join the team, but I 
learned how inexperienced I am as a D-Wheeler.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.720
Pull yourself together!  No one's perfect!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.830
Me, Jack and Yusei are still inexperienced.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:18.370
Dueling is fun because we're 
inexperienced and help each other.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.470
Let's root for Yusei.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.440
Do your best, Yusei!

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.350
Yusei!

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.780
Andore has 1300 life points left.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:38.530
And Team Unicorn's Breo and Jean 
each have 4000 life points!

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:47.070
In order for Team 5D's to win in a comeback, 
Yusei has to take away 9300 life points on his own!

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:50.810
Facing three opponents is exhausting.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:57.860
I was a bit worried when she summoned 
Stardust Dragon, but it was nothing.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:06.470
But in the end, we wasted 4 Speed Counters, 
and Stardust Dragon remains on their field.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.930
Aki Izayoi fought well for an amateur.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.770
But putting up a good fight is meaningless.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:18.540
Now what will you do, Yusei Fudo?

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:20.440
Duel!

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.030
My turn!

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.170
I summon Max Warrior!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:35.520
Battle!  Stardust Dragon 
attacks Thunder Unicorn!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.220
Shooting Sonic!

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.700
Max Warrior attacks you directly!

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.720
Max Warrior's direct attack 
heads towards Andore!

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.160
If this succeeds, Yusei wins!

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.080
He did it!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.520
This will be Team 5D's first victory!

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.020
When Thunder Unicorn is 
destroyed in battle, it's

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.330
Special Summoned in attack position 
during that Battle Phase.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.780
It's removed from play at 
the end of the Battle Phase.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.840
Thunder Unicorn has that effect?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.110
No way!

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.410
Don't worry!

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.520
Yusei already prepared for this.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:24.530
When Max Warrior attacks your monster, it 
gains 400 attack points during the Damage Step.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.650
Our data is correct.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.930
He anticipated our plans, so he's 
trying to destroy our monster.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:31.830
I see.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:35.720
He won't let us keep a monster, even 
if it means mutual destruction.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.220
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.650
Team 5D's counterattack has finally started.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:54.060
Andore's monster is destroyed, and 
Yusei's Stardust Dragon is still alive!

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:58.100
How will Andore fight back 
against this situation?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.270
My turn!

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:05.350
Andore has many Speed Counters again.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.860
He has End of the Storm in his hand.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.170
Will Andore use that card this time?

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:20.890
When you have 10 or more Speed Counters, End 
of the Storm destroys all monsters on the field.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:27.070
For every destroyed monster, that monster's 
controller takes 300 points of damage.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:30.720
I see!  There are only monsters 
on Yusei's side of the field!

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.880
Only Yusei will take damage!

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.140
This is a battle worth 
watching.  Right, Breo?

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.230
Andore and Yusei.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:48.000
Usually, I'd enjoy watching a 
clash between two genius duelists.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:55.210
This is a team battle, not a one-on-one duel.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.260
My strategy is for the team!

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:59.580
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:00.720
What?

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.960
How unexpected!

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:08.570
Andore only set two cards and ended his turn!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.740
He set his entire hand?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:14.770
One of the two cards is End of the Storm.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.340
This is your chance, Yusei!

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:20.000
Attack him directly with 
Stardust Dragon next turn!

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.430
No, he must have a plan.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:30.920
I see!  Andore set End of the Storm so that 
he could pass it on to his next teammate.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:34.940
Instead of activating End 
of the Storm to take away my

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:39.870
life points, he's keeping it 
as a trump card for later.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.890
I won't let him do that!

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.550
My turn!

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:50.630
By destroying one spell or 
trap card on the field, I

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.740
can summon Card Breaker from 
my hand in attack position.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:58.180
Which card is End of the Storm?

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:02.830
One card is a decoy so that I 
won't destroy End of the Storm.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.790
I have to take the risk!

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.380
I destroy the card on the right!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.890
He did it!  He destroyed End of the Storm!

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:20.080
The next player won't get that card!

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.880
That's our Yusei!

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.800
Go!  Attack him directly this time!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.820
Gracias!  You helped me 
by destroying that one!

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:30.510
What?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.750
It's going exactly as planned.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.980
It was a fun duel, but now is the time.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.130
What?

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.580
My job is done.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.870
As Team Unicorn's vanguard, my 
final task is to activate this.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.630
I flip over the trap card Magic Charge!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:56.850
When your card effect destroys a spell card 
on my field, we both take 2000 points of damage.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:06.750
Yusei!

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:10.600
Whoa!  Andore destroyed himself!

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:16.880
Team 5D's gained their long-awaited 
victory at a huge cost!

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:21.500
Yusei lost half his life 
points in the final blow!

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.400
He tricked us!  He planned 
that from the start!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:32.190
He set End of the Storm so that 
Yusei would destroy a set card.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:32.990
Yeah.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:41.130
And since Andore has 0 life points, Yusei 
has to skip his Battle Phase and end his turn.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:46.590
Incredible.  Not only did he defeat Jack and 
Aki, but he cut Yusei's life points in half.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:51.850
Andore took 10,000 life 
points away on his own.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.860
I leave the rest to you, Breo.

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.290
Leave it to me, Andore!

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:06.470
Breo, don't try to beat him on your own.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:10.190
I'll do what's best for 
the team.  Don't worry.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.180
You did okay, Andore.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:20.500
Just okay?  That's not very nice.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.710
It was average for you.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.500
Your expectations are too high.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:35.600
The duel restarts with Team Unicorn's 
second wheeler Breo's turn!

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:40.120
How will he duel using what 
Andore left behind on his field?

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.160
Duel!

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.320
Yusei...

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.030
Master Atlas!

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.020
Jack!

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.880
Don't worry, Jack.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:07.970
Yusei will surely win.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:09.380
Surely...

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:17.540
I'm impressed that Andore could duel 
so aggressively among the cheers.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.430
A true genius is on a different level.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:27.210
Oops.  I have to stay focused.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:30.320
I have to do my duty properly.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.410
My turn!

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:37.500
Team Unicorn has maximum Speed Counters.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:41.430
They can use whatever Speed 
Spells they want again.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:45.470
What type of duelist is Breo?

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:48.970
I don't know.  I have no data on him.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.600
Why not?  You're supposed to check him out!

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.090
Be reasonable.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:13:01.670
Up to now, Andore always defeated all three 
opponents, so the other two never battled.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.340
No way!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:09.790
Does that mean Team Unicorn's 
other two members are weak?

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.650
Yeah!  That's probably true!

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:15.440
That's why Andore had to win by himself.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.580
What will he use against me?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:25.140
I summon the Tuner Monster Bicorn 
Re'em in defense position!

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.590
A Tuner?  Is he Synchro Summoning?

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.600
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.300
What?

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.580
He only strengthened his defense?

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:46.280
Good!  Yusei will have many Speed Counters 
next turn, so it'll no longer be one-sided!

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.790
My turn!

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:52.220
I only have 2000 life points left.

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:54.400
Can I attack without caution?

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.720
Yusei is perplexed.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:58.480
Yeah.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:04.300
In order to find out what he's planning, 
I must duel the way I want to!

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:07.330
I summon Dash Warrior in attack position!

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.340
Battle!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.060
Dash Warrior attacks Bicorn Re'em!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:24.260
When Dash Warrior attacks, its attack points 
triple until the end of the Battle Phase.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:28.210
Just like the data said!  The 
Counter Trap Negate Attack!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.740
He protected his Tuner 
Monster using Negate Attack.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.820
Is he actually preparing to Synchro Summon?

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:48.140
Should I use Speed World 2's effect 
now and destroy that monster?

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:53.550
Or should I stop the Synchro Monster 
that Breo will summon in the future?

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.890
He's thinking hard to figure 
out what Breo is planning.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:02.940
If he acts carelessly, he'll put his 
few remaining life points in danger.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:06.190
In comparison, we have plenty of life points.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.250
This is what makes team battles scary.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.460
The side at the disadvantage must 
focus more and more on defense.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:16.800
I switch Card Breaker to defense 
position and end my turn.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:20.810
The more Breo forces his 
opponent to defend, the

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:25.110
more his opponent gets trapped 
inside an inescapable pit.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:27.250
My turn.

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:30.780
I summon Mine Mole!

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:38.340
Level 4 Bicorn Re'em tunes Level 3 Mine Mole!

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.140
As expected, he's Synchro Summoning!

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:47.770
Soaring thunder, slice the sea of clouds 
and pierce the land with your hooves!

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:49.230
Synchro Summon!

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.300
Roar, Voltic Bicorn!

00:15:54.340 --> 00:16:02.030
When Bicorn Re'em is used as Synchro Material, 
two cards in your deck are sent to the graveyard.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:13.010
And when Mine Mole is used to Synchro Summon a 
Beast-Type monster, I can draw one card from my deck!

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:19.430
That monster has the same number of 
attack points as Stardust Dragon.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.960
He's not weak!  This is bad!

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:28.630
He might use Speed World 2 
to destroy Stardust Dragon.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.930
What's he going to do?

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:32.990
Do it, Breo!

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:37.670
Teach them what it really 
means to battle as a team.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:44.840
Jean, you're my savior who 
brought me to the big stage.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.920
I'll pass you the baton 
in the best situation!

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:51.530
Battle!  Voltic Bicorn attacks!

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:56.700
That's what I would've done in the past.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:03.320
Go!

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.270
Infernal Dragon attacks you directly!

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:14.180
I was the king of the mountain.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:17.810
I thought I was number one.  The only one.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.610
I was conceited and wrong.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.600
Breo, you're the best!

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:35.080
I only belong to you.

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:38.340
I dedicate this victory to you.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.780
Meeting Jean and Andore changed me.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:50.880
Hey!

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:55.590
This is my practice course.  
Do that somewhere else.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:59.830
That's strange.  This is a public road.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:07.130
I'll prove it to you by dueling, but 
that means you'll face a lot of pain.

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:13.770
Fine.  I'll take you on.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.900
Breo!

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:21.670
Hurry up and get rid of him!

00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:23.540
It'll end quickly.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.000
I learned that I wasn't number one.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:44.790
Hey!

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.630
You're strong.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.720
I like strong men.

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.610
I have no interest in frivolous women.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:01.680
What?  You're stuck up!

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:10.530
Funny, isn't it?

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:12.640
Laugh at me.

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:17.150
Point at me, clutch your stomach and laugh.

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:21.930
I'm Jean.  He's Andore.

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.650
Your name is Breo, right?

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:32.240
You have the talent that 
we've been looking for.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:34.380
Will you join us?

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:37.270
Are you making fun of me?

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:41.010
I lost pathetically!  I have no talent!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:45.500
You dueling is raw, but it shines.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.710
You just haven't realized it yet.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:53.480
Will you trust me with your talent?

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:58.440
Aren't you bored of battling alone?

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:02.160
Join our team and go further!

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:20.290
I was alone and self-satisfied 
back then, but no longer.

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:25.280
I'm proud that I'm part of Team Unicorn!

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.810
This is the best tactic to show my pride!

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.400
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:32.470
It's finally coming!

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:39.400
I remove 10 Speed Counters to 
destroy one card on the field!

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:42.850
I destroy Voltic Bicorn!

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:43.680
What?

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.100
Not Stardust Dragon?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.260
He's destroying his own monster?

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.670
What is he thinking?

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.500
When Voltic Bicorn is destroyed, we both send

00:20:57.510 --> 00:21:00.750
cards in our decks to our 
graveyards equal to its Level.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.750
Voltic Bicorn is Level 7!

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.310
Send seven cards in your 
deck to the graveyard!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.900
Seven cards?

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:16.610
This strategy is...

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:18.380
Hey, he's...

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.770
Breo's strategy is to...

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:23.370
They finally noticed.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:30.840
I let End of the Storm be destroyed because 
I didn't need to leave it for Breo.

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:35.250
Because Stardust Dragon 
isn't a threat to his deck.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.240
This is deck destruction!

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:13.010
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:18.020
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:22.920
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:27.930
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:32.800
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:39.740
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.740 --> 00:22:43.570
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:49.450
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:53.350
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:59.320
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.320 --> 00:23:02.260
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.260 --> 00:23:04.500
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:09.170
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:12.040
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:15.510
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:18.740
At our special place
